cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it with the metadata below (and the paper it supports, once published)."
type: software
title: "SOTHE-P2: code and data for the Paper-2 computations of the SOTHE project"
abstract: >-
  Python (NumPy, Matplotlib) implementation of the numerical results of the second SOTHE paper on solitonic
  event horizons in dispersive media: Bogoliubov-de Gennes spectra about the stationary third-order-dispersion
  soliton, radiative loss of the soliton core from direct integration of the generalized nonlinear
  Schroedinger equation, the kinematic surface gravity with its thermal and entanglement layers, the data
  products and the figures. A rewrite of the project's MATLAB programs; runs on a laptop or on a SLURM cluster.
